From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:22:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rp2040: Keep CAN encoding outside the IRQ lock

The demand-driven transmit wakeup change masked interrupts around
can2040_transmit().  That function also computes the CRC and stuffs
all frame bits, unnecessarily delaying the CAN PIO and step timer
interrupts throughout message preparation.

Mask interrupts only while checking queue capacity and publishing the
waiter.  Producers run in cooperative tasks, while the interrupt only
removes queued frames, so a free slot cannot be consumed between the
check and the subsequent can2040_transmit() call.  Encoding can thus
run with interrupts restored without reopening the lost-wakeup race.

A native harness checks that encoding runs with interrupts enabled,
full queues register a waiter, a completion immediately after restoring
interrupts wakes that waiter, and unneeded completions do not wake the
task.  It fails on the previous interrupt-masked encoding.  USB-CAN
firmware builds pass for both RP2040 and RP2350.  Frame encoding and
wire contents are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit c3c9c312d6c3d324e6fa99b86bde2828c9549bee)

diff --git a/src/rp2040/can.c b/src/rp2040/can.c
index e61c73ff..70b26946 100644
--- a/src/rp2040/can.c
+++ b/src/rp2040/can.c
@@ -30,24 +30,19 @@ static uint8_t can_tx_waiting;
 int
 canhw_send(struct canbus_msg *msg)
 {
-    /*
-     * can2040 reports every successful transmit through its callback, but the
-     * routing task needs that notification only after can2040_transmit() has
-     * rejected a frame because its four-entry software queue is full.  Record
-     * that condition with PIO interrupts masked.  The library advances its
-     * consumer index and invokes the callback in that interrupt, so publishing
-     * the waiter before interrupts are restored closes the completion-versus-
-     * rejection race without changing can2040's queue implementation.
-     */
+    // Publish a capacity waiter atomically with the full-queue check.  Only
+    // tasks add frames, and interrupts can only free slots, so available
+    // capacity remains available after restoring interrupts.  Keep can2040's
+    // CRC calculation and bit stuffing outside this critical section.
     irqstatus_t flag = irq_save();
-    int ret = can2040_transmit(&cbus, (void*)msg);
-    if (ret < 0) {
+    if (!can2040_check_transmit(&cbus)) {
         writeb(&can_tx_waiting, 1);
         irq_restore(flag);
         return -1;
     }
     writeb(&can_tx_waiting, 0);
     irq_restore(flag);
+    can2040_transmit(&cbus, (void*)msg);
     return CANMSG_DATA_LEN(msg);
 }
 
